From 41ae9ea6822a095d1f9bba6d528b0228a06d2d6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivory <contact@ivory.cafe>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 12:27:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/21] Publish capture artifacts through a verified shared
 directory

Consume the prepared directory capability, reopen O_PATH as the same verified inode for directory fsync, and atomically publish setgid-inherited 0660 files without recreating trusted subdirectories.

Constraint: Canonical files must be immediately writable by ext_data_rw while remaining non-world-accessible
Rejected: Fsync directly on O_PATH | the kernel returns EBADF after rename and falsely degrades the run
Confidence: high
Scope-risk: moderate
Directive: Verify owner, group, mode, device, and inode before retaining any prepared directory FD
Tested: r0dump_FileTest 25/25; art_runtime_tests and com.android.art builds; Coolapk produced 11 artifacts and 50 records without run_degraded
Not-tested: no full platform build was required
Change-Id: Ia5703a2d1d92222b9322ee85e9945812cbce2bd7
